#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0106 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "Adapted from -valid_strain_in_ts-DM with ONE change: the TS STRAIN row's TSVAL is BLANK. ts_parameter_value returns the first key-matching row's TSVAL, which is missing, so it yields null and empty($ts_strain) is TRUE. Pins the sheet Rule cell verbatim -- 'Record with TSPARMCD = \"STRAIN\" is present in TS AND TSVAL ^= null for that record' -- i.e. a present-but-empty parameter does not satisfy it. *** version=3-0 is LOAD-BEARING. M3-D8 restricted this rule's Standards block to the single (SENDIG, 3.0) entry the sheet supports -- row 526 is SEND106's ONLY row -- so from v3.1 onward only the .1 successor ships. Before that fix the base co-shipped with its replacement in five packages and CONTRADICTED it: a conformant v3.1+ study declaring the strain in TX was silent under 0106.1 and reported by 0106, which has no TX operand at all. ***"
#library standard=sendig version=3-0
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=001
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SUBJID  type=Char label="Subject Identifier for the Study"
col SPECIES type=Char label="Species"
col STRAIN  type=Char label="Strain/Substrain"
col SEX     type=Char label="Sex"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 001 | RAT |  | M | LD | Low Dose
S1 | DM | 002 | 002 | RAT |  | M | MD | Mid Dose
S1 | DM | 003 | 003 | RAT |  | F | HD | High Dose
---

dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | TITLE   | Trial Title | 28-Day Oral Toxicity Study
S1 | TS | 2 | SPECIES | Species     | RAT
S1 | TS | 3 | STRAIN | Strain/Substrain |
---
